{"vid":"2rcyRVVUkJg","source":"2rcyRVVUkJg.en-en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":2.9,"txt":"You're learning with nine to five English - business English for the workplace"},{"t":14.9,"txt":"Hi Tim here with another"},{"t":18.6,"txt":"nine-to-five English lesson"},{"t":21.3,"txt":"Today we're going to learn how to make generalizations in English"},{"t":29.1,"txt":"don't you hate it when people say things like"},{"t":33.4,"txt":"Americans are rude. I mean not all"},{"t":37.6,"txt":"Americans are rude and people in other countries are rude, too. It's simply not helpful to say"},{"t":45.7,"txt":"Something is true of a whole group of people"},{"t":49.4,"txt":"When it's negative like that, it feels wrong"},{"t":54,"txt":"But it can be helpful to describe a group of people as long as we're clear that it's not"},{"t":61.8,"txt":"Everyone we're talking about"},{"t":64.2,"txt":"we call this a"},{"t":66.9,"txt":"generalization"},{"t":68.4,"txt":"for example many of my friends work in finance"},{"t":73.9,"txt":"I'm making a generalization"},{"t":77.1,"txt":"about my friends and"},{"t":79.5,"txt":"It doesn't have to be people if I say"},{"t":84,"txt":"Most of our online sales come from Europe. I'm"},{"t":88.8,"txt":"generalizing about sales"},{"t":92,"txt":"Let's try making a few"},{"t":94.9,"txt":"generalizations like this"},{"t":97,"txt":"Listen to each example then repeat it for yourself"},{"t":101.9,"txt":"Ready, let's get started"},{"t":106.7,"txt":"Very little of our business comes through online sales actually"},{"t":116.8,"txt":"Many of the customer concerns are about delivery times"},{"t":126.2,"txt":"Most of the people i've talked - like the new website on"},{"t":134.5,"txt":"The whole our employees are pretty happy with their jobs"},{"t":144.8,"txt":"Did you hear that expression on the whole"},{"t":148.9,"txt":"That's a useful phrase. That means in general"},{"t":154.5,"txt":"you're not talking about everything or"},{"t":158.7,"txt":"everyone"},{"t":160,"txt":"just overall or"},{"t":162.7,"txt":"mainly"},{"t":164.2,"txt":"besides phrases like on the whole you can make this type of"},{"t":170.2,"txt":"generalization with words like most and"},{"t":174.4,"txt":"little"},{"t":176.1,"txt":"now we don't only generalize about how much or how many"},{"t":182.8,"txt":"we also"},{"t":184.2,"txt":"generalize about what happens"},{"t":187.6,"txt":"For example, you might say something like the department budget is normally reviewed by our manager"},{"t":196.3,"txt":"that word"},{"t":198,"txt":"normally tells us that it doesn't always happen, but"},{"t":203.2,"txt":"It usually does"},{"t":206.1,"txt":"let's practice some examples of"},{"t":209.3,"txt":"generalizing about things that happen"},{"t":212.6,"txt":"Remember to repeat the examples after you hear them"},{"t":219.3,"txt":"Generally speaking. We see higher sales in the summer months"},{"t":229.4,"txt":"Nine times out of ten customers. Give us great feedback"},{"t":239.5,"txt":"Normally our new employees go through a training program"},{"t":248.8,"txt":"In most cases we finish our projects ahead of schedule"},{"t":259.6,"txt":"So besides normally you can use expressions like in most cases and"},{"t":269.3,"txt":"Generally speaking and the other expression we heard is"},{"t":274.5,"txt":"Nine times out of ten. That sounds pretty exact. Doesn't it?"},{"t":280.2,"txt":"But it really just means in most cases"},{"t":284.2,"txt":"We don't really mean exactly ninety percent of the time"},{"t":289.6,"txt":"This leads me to talk about how often"},{"t":293.5,"txt":"something happens"},{"t":295.3,"txt":"that's something we can generalize about as well and"},{"t":300,"txt":"It's very important. Which words you use you want to be"},{"t":306.9,"txt":"Somewhat accurate for example, are you late for work usually?"},{"t":313.6,"txt":"sometimes"},{"t":315,"txt":"or"},{"t":316.7,"txt":"rarely"},{"t":317.8,"txt":"these are"},{"t":319.5,"txt":"frequency words"},{"t":321.3,"txt":"If you don't use a frequency word"},{"t":325,"txt":"Then you are"},{"t":326.3,"txt":"suggesting that something always or"},{"t":329.3,"txt":"never happens and"},{"t":331.5,"txt":"That might not be true"},{"t":334.7,"txt":"Let's try some of these expressions for generalizing about how often something happens"},{"t":342.4,"txt":"Once again, repeat the examples after you hear them"},{"t":349.5,"txt":"People don't usually buy something on their first visit"},{"t":359,"txt":"More often than not we run out of paper before the end of the month"},{"t":369.1,"txt":"It's pretty rare that people complain about our service"},{"t":378,"txt":"Our staff meetings often lasts more than 90 minutes"},{"t":388.4,"txt":"You probably already know the word often but what do you think more often than not"},{"t":396.5,"txt":"means"},{"t":397.8,"txt":"It actually just means more than 50% of the time"},{"t":403.9,"txt":"We also heard the adjective rare that's made from the word"},{"t":410.4,"txt":"rarely meaning not often"},{"t":414.2,"txt":"some other frequency words have adjective forms such as"},{"t":419.9,"txt":"usually which becomes"},{"t":422.9,"txt":"usual but others such as"},{"t":425.9,"txt":"often don't"},{"t":429.1,"txt":"Okay, so we've practiced some expressions for generalizing"},{"t":434.3,"txt":"about how many about how things happen and"},{"t":439,"txt":"how often"},{"t":440.5,"txt":"But how does this sound in a?"},{"t":444,"txt":"conversation"},{"t":445.1,"txt":"Let's listen to a short"},{"t":447.2,"txt":"dialogue between"},{"t":448.8,"txt":"justine, and andy they're talking about andy's customers and"},{"t":454.8,"txt":"products"},{"t":456,"txt":"Let's listen"},{"t":459.6,"txt":"So, where are your customers located"},{"t":462.9,"txt":"Most of them are in Canada and the US and are they happy with your products? Well, it's pretty rare that we get any complaints"},{"t":473.7,"txt":"That's pretty simple, right"},{"t":476.7,"txt":"When justine asks about the location of andy's customers"},{"t":482.1,"txt":"he says that most of them are in canada and"},{"t":487.6,"txt":"the US"},{"t":489.5,"txt":"he's"},{"t":490.8,"txt":"generalizing about how many"},{"t":493.1,"txt":"Then he says that it's rare that they get complaints about their products. That's"},{"t":501.1,"txt":"generalizing about how often something happens"},{"t":505.1,"txt":"Makes sense, right?"},{"t":508.1,"txt":"Now it's your turn to practice"},{"t":511.1,"txt":"Will repeat the dialogue but this time we're going to be out the second speakers words"},{"t":518.6,"txt":"You will have to say those parts"},{"t":521.4,"txt":"yourself"},{"t":522.9,"txt":"Remember to say that most of the customers are in Canada and the US"},{"t":530.8,"txt":"Then say it's pretty rare to get complaints"},{"t":537.7,"txt":"So, where are your customers located"},{"t":546.9,"txt":"And are they happy with your products"},{"t":558,"txt":"Alright that's all for this lesson"},{"t":560.9,"txt":"we've learned some great ways to generalize about how many about what happens and"},{"t":569.7,"txt":"About how often things happen"},{"t":572.9,"txt":"We'll be back soon with some more"},{"t":576.2,"txt":"useful English expressions"},{"t":578.8,"txt":"Until then so long and happy learning"}],"words":[{"t":2.86,"w":"You're"},{"t":2.86,"w":"learning"},{"t":2.86,"w":"with"},{"t":2.86,"w":"nine"},{"t":2.86,"w":"to"},{"t":2.86,"w":"five"},{"t":2.86,"w":"English"},{"t":2.86,"w":"-"},{"t":2.86,"w":"business"},{"t":2.86,"w":"English"},{"t":2.86,"w":"for"},{"t":2.86,"w":"the"},{"t":2.86,"w":"workplace"},{"t":14.89,"w":"Hi"},{"t":14.89,"w":"Tim"},{"t":14.89,"w":"here"},{"t":14.89,"w":"with"},{"t":14.89,"w":"another"},{"t":18.61,"w":"nine-to-five"},{"t":18.61,"w":"English"},{"t":18.61,"w":"lesson"},{"t":21.31,"w":"Today"},{"t":21.31,"w":"we're"},{"t":21.31,"w":"going"},{"t":21.31,"w":"to"},{"t":21.31,"w":"learn"},{"t":21.31,"w":"how"},{"t":21.31,"w":"to"},{"t":21.31,"w":"make"},{"t":21.31,"w":"generalizations"},{"t":21.31,"w":"in"},{"t":21.31,"w":"English"},{"